# Cursor rules for GlobeTrotter

Full rules live in `docs/AI_RULES.md`, read that file in full before generating code in this repo. This file is a pointer, not a substitute, do not skip reading the real document.

Cursor also loads `.cursor/rules/ai-rules.mdc` on every prompt (`alwaysApply: true`). Keep that file in sync with `docs/AI_RULES.md` if the rules change.

Summary, the full doc has the detail behind each of these:

1. Do not hallucinate. Verify libraries against `requirements.txt`/`package.json`, verify model fields against `backend/app/models/`, verify route signatures against `backend/app/routers/`, never invent an env var or API method.
2. Stay in scope. Check `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`'s ownership table before editing a router outside your assigned module. Model changes require a matching Alembic migration in the same change.
3. Security is non-negotiable. No hardcoded secrets. Every user-data route checks resource ownership. Every admin route is server-side role-gated. No raw SQL string interpolation. No `allow_origins=["*"]` with credentials enabled.
4. If unsure, say so, do not produce a confident guess.
